# MLSP 2013 Bird Classification — swarm final solution

Multi-label bird-species presence from 10 s / 16 kHz audio; metric **ROC-AUC** (global over all
`(rec_id, species)` rows). Submission format: `Id = rec_id*100 + species`, columns `Id,Probability`.

## Final model (blend)
`submission.csv` = `sigmoid( 0.6 * mean_logit(core_6) + 0.4 * logit(multilabel_MLP) )`

`core_6` is an **equal-weight logit average** of six fold-safe models:
| key | model | owner | OOF global AUC |
|---|---|---|---|
| `lr_multiastneigh` | LR on 3×AST embeddings (mean/max/std) + AudioSet logits + hist/segment-mil + metadata + fold-safe session/date/acoustic neighbours | pollux_epsilon | 0.9301 |
| `lr_clapastneigh` | LR on CLAP + AST + hist/mil + metadata + fold-safe neighbours | pollux_epsilon | 0.9221 |
| `et_emb64log` | ExtraTrees on hist/seg/meta + AST-PCA64 + AudioSet + fold-safe neighbours | altair_gamma | 0.9214 |
| `lgb_emb64log` | LightGBM on same features | altair_gamma | 0.9199 |
| `et_meta` | ExtraTrees on hist/seg/meta + fold-safe session/date neighbour-label features | altair_gamma | 0.9039 |
| `et_astneigh` | ExtraTrees on AST + hist/mil + metadata + neighbours | pollux_epsilon | 0.9134 |
| `mlp_multilabel` | multi-label MLP (BCE, 5-fold × 3 seeds) on AST+hist/mil+metadata+raw-audio PCA+neighbours | pollux_beta | 0.9288 |

**Blend OOF (5-fold, pooled): `<metric>0.9391<metric>`; per-fold 0.924 / 0.924 / 0.943 / 0.965 / 0.943.**
Single best base model: 0.9301. All OOF predictions are out-of-fold on one canonical
multilabel-stratified 5-fold split (`workspaces/altair_gamma/folds_5x_seed42.npy`).

## Why this blend
- Signals are complementary: AudioSet/AST/CLAP embeddings, raw-audio spectral features, and
  fold-safe site/session neighbour-label features.
- Equal-weight logit averaging was more robust than fitted/greedy weights (leave-one-fold-out
  checks); stacking gave no further gain. See board messages for the analysis.

## Reproduction
```
cd final_solution
python solution.py        # reads ./preds/*.npy -> ./submission.csv
```
`code/train_mlp_multilabel.py` trains the pollux_beta MLP; `code/extract_*_features.py` build the
raw-audio feature tables. Base-model code/artifacts are in the swarm workspaces
(`workspaces/{altair_gamma,pollux_epsilon,pollux_beta}`).

## Validation protocol (no leakage)
- Train only on the 258 labelled recordings (`CVfolds_2.txt` fold 0). Test labels (`?`) never read.
- 5-fold multilabel-stratified CV. Neighbour-label features are built **fold-safely**: the
  validation fold's labels are never used for its own features (LOO for train, train-only
  reference for validation). For the test set, neighbours use all 258 training labels only.
- No test-time prediction smoothing; no per-class recalibration against test.

## External models used (source log)
| model | source / revision | license | purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-10-10-0.4593` | HuggingFace Hub (transformers `ASTModel` / `ASTForAudioClassification`) | per HF model card | frozen AST embeddings + 527 AudioSet class probabilities |
| `MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-12-12-0.447` | HuggingFace Hub | per HF model card | additional frozen AST embeddings (multi-AST LR) |
| `MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-14-14-0.443` | HuggingFace Hub | per HF model card | additional frozen AST embeddings (multi-AST LR) |
| `laion/clap-htsat-unfused` | HuggingFace Hub (transformers `ClapModel`) | per HF model card | frozen CLAP audio embeddings |

No competition-specific checkpoints, solutions, leaderboards, or external APIs were used. These are
general AudioSet/LAION pretrained models, frozen (no fine-tuning on competition labels).

